result: 'All 5 crash-safety soundness bugs fixed and un-ignored in tests/crash_safety.rs
  (37/37 pass): (1) take-inside-loop now a compile error via check_loop_body_moves
  in typer (For/SimFor/Loop); (2) bound Result match ICE fixed by resolving misclassified
  Param annotations to declared Enum/Struct in monomorphize_named_annotation + handling
  Param/TypeVar payload size in declare_tagged_union; (3) string slice OOB trap (start<=end
  && end<=len); (4) char_at OOB trap (idx<len); (5) oversized-shift trap (count<bitwidth)
  for Shl/Shr/Ushr.'
description: 'Five bugs discovered while building the crash-safety suite; each has
  an #[ignore]d test in tests/crash_safety.rs documenting desired behavior — un-ignore
  as fixed:

  1. `take` inside a loop body compiles and double-frees at runtime (free(): invalid
  pointer, exit 134). Should be a compile error: take_inside_loop_is_compile_error.

  2. Binding a Result to a variable then matching ICEs: `unresolved type parameter
  ''E'' reached codegen` (src/codegen/types.rs:45 monomorphization bug): bound_result_match_does_not_ice.
  Also blocks .unwrap()/.to_int() method resolution on bound Result values (''unknown
  method unwrap'').

  3. s.slice(start, end) with end > len reads OOB heap memory (src/codegen/string_ops.rs
  string_slice has no bounds check): string_slice_oob_is_checked.

  4. s.char_at(idx) past length reads OOB memory (string_char_at, no bounds check):
  string_char_at_oob_is_checked.

  5. Shift count >= bit width produces LLVM poison (1 << 70 returns garbage): oversized_shift_is_defined.
  Trap or mask per documented semantics.

  Definition of done: all 5 tests un-ignored and passing, zero warnings, full cargo
  test green.'
